data.content:
In .NET 11 (EF Core 11), the Cosmos DB provider **removes sync-over-async support entirely**. The opt-in configuration (`EnableSyncOverAsync` or the `CosmosOptionsExtension` flag) no longer exists.

**What breaks:** Every synchronous LINQ call — `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, `SaveChanges()` — will throw an `InvalidOperationException` at runtime because the Cosmos provider no longer wraps async calls in sync blocking.

**Fix:** Convert to async equivalents:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `Add()` is still synchronous (it's an in-memory operation) — only the query/save execution must be async.
- You'll need to propagate `async/await` up through your call stack (controllers, services, etc.).
- Remove the old `EnableSyncOverAsync` configuration — it will cause a compile error in EF Core 11.
